id: pm-slack-standup-20gw
title: The .cmd shim resolvePmBin selects on win32 cannot be launched by its only caller
description: "resolvePmBin deliberately returns the node_modules/.bin/pm.cmd batch shim on win32 because Windows cannot execute the extensionless POSIX shim. But fetchAllItems passes that return value straight to spawnSync with no shell/command-processor option. Since the CVE-2024-27980 hardening landed (Node 18.20+, 20.12+), Node refuses to execute .cmd/.bat via spawnSync without a shell and fails with EINVAL. So on the exact platform the .cmd branch exists to support, every pm list-all read fails to spawn and every standup export/post aborts, even though the project-local CLI is installed. The resolution decision (use the .cmd) and the launch decision (how to spawn) live in different places and disagree."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-15T10:04:21.035Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-15T10:14:34.376Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-15T10:14:34.362Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-15T10:14:34.362Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
severity: high
resolution: "resolvePmBin now returns a PmLaunch {command, prefixArgs} built by the new pmLaunchPlan(bin, platform): on win32 the spawn targets the ComSpec command processor (cmd.exe fallback) with [\"/d\",\"/s\",\"/c\", bin] ahead of the pm arguments; everywhere else it spawns the resolved binary directly with an empty prefix, byte-for-byte the previous POSIX invocation. fetchAllItems consumes that plan for both its default and its string parameter (strings normalize through the same pmLaunchPlan), so the resolution decision and the launch decision can no longer disagree. No shell:true anywhere; arguments remain discrete argv elements with windowsVerbatimArguments:false so Node quotes each one itself."
expected_result: "The .cmd shim resolvePmBin selects on win32 is launched through a command processor, so a project-local pm read succeeds on Windows; POSIX launches are unchanged; no argument metacharacter is ever interpreted by a shell."
actual_result: "Verified without a Windows box by platform injection: exact argv asserted for win32+.cmd (cmd.exe /d /s /c <pm.cmd> --path ... list-all --json --include-body), win32+extensionless, and linux (bare shim, no prefix); a real-subprocess test passes a root containing space & quote | pipe and observes it arrive as one discrete argv element. Revert checks: full index.ts revert fails the suite at import; surgical revert of the ComSpec wrapping fails the four launch tests. npm run release:check green; coverage 89.05/87.43/90.35 (baseline 88.64/87.07/90.27)."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
