comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T10:13:06.965Z",pi-agent,"Root cause confirmed by inspecting every spawn site: index.ts has exactly one child-process call that consumes resolvePmBin's value — fetchAllItems' spawnSync (no spawn/execFile anywhere else). The resolver picked pm.cmd on win32 while the caller spawned that path directly with no command processor; since the CVE-2024-27980 hardening (Node 18.20+/20.12+) spawnSync refuses .cmd/.bat without a shell and fails EINVAL, every standup read aborted on Windows.\n\nFix collapses the two decisions into one place. New pmLaunchPlan(bin, platform) returns {command, prefixArgs}: on win32 spawn ComSpec (default cmd.exe) with [\"/d\",\"/s\",\"/c\", bin]; everywhere else spawn bin directly with an empty prefix — byte-for-byte the old POSIX invocation. resolvePmBin(moduleUrl, platform) now returns that PmLaunch (platform injectable, same pattern as moduleUrl), and fetchAllItems accepts a PmLaunch or a path string, normalizing strings through the same pmLaunchPlan so no caller can bypass the launch decision. No shell:true anywhere: arguments stay discrete argv elements with windowsVerbatimArguments:false, so Node quotes each one itself and metacharacters reach pm as data.\n\nTests: exact argv for win32+.cmd, win32+extensionless, and linux; ComSpec honored plus cmd.exe fallback; bare-pm PATH fallback wrapped on win32; and a real-subprocess metacharacter test (a root containing space, &, \", and |) proving it arrives as ONE argv element. Revert experiments: a full revert of index.ts fails the suite at import (pmLaunchPlan no longer exported); a surgical revert of just the ComSpec wrapping fails 4 tests with command collapsing to the bare pm.cmd path and the /d /s /c prefix missing. npm run release:check green; coverage 89.05/87.43/90.35 (baseline 88.64/87.07/90.27), thresholds untouched.\n"
files[2]{path,scope}:
  index.ts,project
  test/fetch-all-items.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,note}:
  npm run coverage,project,"132 tests pass; includes exact per-platform launch argv (win32+.cmd,win32+extensionless,linux),ComSpec honoring + fallback,PATH-fallback wrapping,and the POSIX metacharacter argv round trip"
close_reason: "pm list-all reads on win32 spawn through ComSpec instead of failing EINVAL on the bare .cmd shim; 132/132 tests pass; release:check green."
